ties, and in the republics of Novgorod and Pskov. Copper money also was turned out." "In the pre-Kievan era cattle and furs had served as mediums of exchange and foreign coins had also been used. In the Kievan centuries metallic money came into general use. Coins were minted from the first half of the eleventh century on into the first quarter of the next century. Small silver bars were also used, and foreign coins had wide circulation."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1908, 'temperature': 0.2})
